   "body": "### Summary\n\nFirst I create a config file specifying a default cooldown period of 1w:\n\n`~/.config/uv/uv.toml`\n\n```toml\n[pip]\nexclude-newer = \"1 week\"\n```\n\nThen create and activate a test venv:\n\n```sh\nuv venv ~/python/venvs/cooldown_test\nsource python/venvs/cooldown_test/bin/activate\n```\n\nNow install a package (that I know has a recent update):\n\n```sh\nuv pip install cryptography\n```\n\nWorks as expected, giving me the slightly dated `cryptography==46.0.6`:\n\n```log\nUsing Python 3.14.2 environment at: python/venvs/cooldown_test\nResolved 3 packages in 127ms\nInstalled 3 packages in 11ms\n + cffi==2.0.0\n + cryptography==46.0.6\n + pycparser==3.0\n```\n\nOh no! There's a recent CVE in that version, best grab the latest one:\n\n```sh\nuv pip install cryptography --exclude-newer=0h\n```\n\nNothing happens \u2639\ufe0f \n\nOK, let's try specifying a version:\n\n```sh\nuv pip install cryptography==46.0.7\n```\n\nHere's where I get the confusing message:\n\n```log\nUsing Python 3.14.2 environment at: python/venvs/cooldown_test\n  \u00d7 No solution found when resolving dependencies:\n  \u2570\u2500\u25b6 Because there is no version of cryptography==46.0.7 and you require\n      cryptography==46.0.7, we can conclude that your requirements are\n      unsatisfiable.\n```\n\nIt should be telling me that it *can* find that version, but won't install it due to `--exclude-newer`\n\nIt turns out that I can work around with:\n\n```sh\nuv pip install cryptography==46.0.7 --exclude-newer=0h\n```\n\nWhich correctly gets me the newer package:\n\n```log\nUsing Python 3.14.2 environment at: python/venvs/cooldown_test\nResolved 3 packages in 12ms\nUninstalled 1 package in 4ms\nInstalled 1 package in 11ms\n - cryptography==46.0.6\n + cryptography==46.0.7\n```\n\n\n### Platform\n\nLinux 6.17.0-19-generic x86_64 GNU/Linux\n\n### Version\n\nuv 0.11.6 (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu)\n\n### Python version\n\nPython 3.14.2",
